{{also|Parry}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|parree}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|parree}}, from {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|*parree}}, {{m|enm|*paree}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|paree||preparation, ceremony, parade}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|parāta||preparation, parade}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|parāre||to ward off, guard, defend, prepare, get ready}}. More at {{l|en|pare}}. The English verb ''to parry'' is taken from the noun.

Alternative etymology derives the verb ''parry'' from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|parez !}}, the imperative form of {{m|fr|parer||to fend off}}, ultimately from the {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|parāre}}. See above.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpæɹi/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|æri|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|parries}}

# A defensive or deflective action; an act of parrying.
# {{lb|en|fencing}} A simple defensive action designed to deflect an attack, performed with the [[forte]] of the blade.

